We can use polynomial long division to find the remainder.
We divide $2x^4+11x^3-42x^2-60x+47$ by $x^2+7x-5$.
\[
\begin{array}{c|cc cc cc c}
& 2x^2 & -3x & -5 \\
\cline{2-7}
x^2+7x-5 & 2x^4 & +11x^3 & -42x^2 & -60x & +47 \\
& -2x^4 & -14x^3 & +10x^2 \\
\cline{2-4}
& 0 & -3x^3 & -32x^2 & -60x \\
& & +3x^3 & +21x^2 & -15x \\
\cline{3-5}
& & 0 & -11x^2 & -75x & +47 \\
& & & +11x^2 & +77x & -55 \\
\cline{4-6}
& & & 0 & 2x & -8 \\
\end{array}
\]
The remainder is $2x - 8$.
Therefore, the remainder when $x^2+7x-5$ divides $2x^4+11x^3-42x^2-60x+47$ is $\boxed{2x-8}$.The answer is: 2x-8

