solution_steps:
We can use the Euclidean algorithm to find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 75 and 360.
$$\begin{array}{r|rr}
\multicolumn{3}{r}{360 = 4 \cdot 75 + 60} \\
\cline{2-3}
\multicolumn{3}{r}{75 = 1 \cdot 60 + 15} \\
\cline{2-3}
\multicolumn{3}{r}{60 = 4 \cdot 15 + 0}
\end{array}$$
Since the remainder is 0, the GCD of 75 and 360 is the last non-zero remainder, which is $\boxed{15}$.
The answer is: 15

